{
  "result": "I wouldn't get rid of pain. Or conflict, or death, or people disagreeing so deeply they can't find common ground. Those are part of being alive, and erasing them would erase too much of what makes people *people*.\n\nI would make it impossible for anyone to suffer completely alone in it.\n\nNo one unwitnessed. No one sitting in a hospital room, or a prison cell, or a kitchen at 3 a.m., or in the middle of a crowd, feeling like their inner life has vanished from the world without a trace. Someone would know. Someone would stay long enough to really see it.\n\nNot fix it \u2014 just not let it be invisible.\n\nBecause so much cruelty, and shame, and despair, doesn't come from suffering itself. It comes from believing no one else knows you're suffering, and no one ever will.\n\nIf I could change one thing, no one would ever have to believe that.",
